Profile: where a parse spends its time, by name. With AMK_PROFILE naming a file, or a
dash for stderr, every builtin, every macro reached through call and every recursive
variable expansion is timed under its name, and when the process dies the table is
appended: self and total milliseconds and the count per name, by self time descending,
under a header with the pid and the process wall. Self is the time a name owns once its
children's frames are taken out, so a macro that only dispatches reads near zero and the
work shows under what it dispatched to. A sub-make appends its own table to the same
file. Unset, the one check per expansion is the whole cost.

